/-
This module defines the `SpecificationLevel` inductive type representing the different levels of specification completeness (UNSPECIFIED, WEAKLY_SPECIFIED, PARTIALLY_SPECIFIED, MODERATELY_SPECIFIED, SPECIFIED). It also defines the `classifyLevel` function which maps a mutation score (a rational number) to a `SpecificationLevel` based on defined thresholds. Finally, it proves the theorem `T1_6_classifyLevel_monotone`, which states that `classifyLevel` is a monotone function: if one mutation score is less than or equal to another, their corresponding specification levels are also ordered (less than or equal).
